      "text": "1. Find the prime factorization of 12: 2^2 * 3\n2. Find the prime factorization of 20: 2^2 * 5\n3. Find the common prime factorization: 2^2\n4. Raise the common prime factorization to the minimum exponent: 2^2 = 4\n5. Answer: \\boxed{4}\n\nHere is another reasoning I can think of about this problem:\n\nWe can also list out the divisors of both 12 and 20: \n\nDivisors of 12: 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 12\nDivisors of 20: 1, 2, 4, 5, 10, 20\n\nThe common divisors of 12 and 20 are: 1, 2, 4\n\nThe greatest common divisor of 12 and 20 is 4, so the final answer is $\\boxed{4}$.",
